From 9f3cc213a6af8790ec113cff37fd30d68a378719 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iasnezhkov <iasnezhkov@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 11:30:31 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] v4l2: register the MPEG-4 and H.263 hardware decoders

check_codec_id() (vdec_vcu_if.c) in our kernel driver recognizes
V4L2_PIX_FMT_MPEG4 and V4L2_PIX_FMT_H263 as real codec IDs, and both
are live-confirmed on the decoder OUTPUT format list alongside
H.264/H.265/VP8/VP9. Stock v4l2_codec2 (H.264/VP8/VP9/HEVC/AV1) has no
concept of either codec at all - not a disabled entry, the VideoCodec
enum itself has no MPEG4/H263 value.

Add both as decoders only, matching this driver own decode-only
control shape: mtk-vcodec-dec.c registers zero profile/level V4L2
controls for any codec (profile/level are bitstream properties vpud
discovers itself, never negotiated up front), so MPEG-4/H.263 decode
slots into the exact same generic, capability-query-with-hardcoded-
fallback path H.264/HEVC/VP9/AV1 already use - no new architecture,
just two more entries in each already-generic VideoCodec switch
(VideoTypes, Common::isValidProfileForCodec, DecodeInterface profile/
level/mime/output-delay tables, V4L2Device pixfmt<->codec mapping) and
two new component names gated by their own product properties.

Encoder-side MPEG-4/H.263 (also real on this hardware per
mtk-vcodec-enc.c, Simple profile default) is intentionally left out of
this series: it needs its own EncodeInterface profile/level wiring and
is lower priority than getting decode and the HEVC encoder gap closed
first. Left for a follow-up patch.

Change-Id: Ia021298897f0900531e0fc8597002f464804610d
